                <pb facs="0899" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.404/1826: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Saltillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-09T08:00:00-06:00">December 9, 1935—8
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I had a conference at Monterrey with Mexican Ambassador to Washington who is en
                    route to that city. He stated that on the previous day he had talked 4 hours
                    with President Cárdenas and discussed agrarian and church and other important
                    questions. He feels that the situation as to each is in much better condition
                    and he thinks more satisfactory. He will reach Washington about the middle of
                    the week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
